            <ArticleTitle>[Mechanism of the anti-inflammatory and analgesic effects of benzofurocaine and voltaren].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>66-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Non-narcotic analgesics benzofurocaine and voltaren (10% of LD50) were shown to exert the protective effect on rats in castor oil-induced diarrhea, to decrease in mice the degree of pain reaction under the influence of acetylcholine, acetic acid and thermic stimulation.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
